Code Red: the PokÉEG in the game (owner, 2026-10-09). A PC screen listing every Pokémon
the player owns (party, then the boxes) and, for the one under the cursor, a look inside
its mind: its type's system, readers learned, Pokédex readers, byte budget, focus, the
last ten turns (hit/miss) and its hot memory. The game asks the page through a mailbox
(struct CodeRedEeg, 164 B) one Pokémon at a time; hot memory is typed on the page.
Menu entries live in patch 003 (PC menu, bedroom PC); this patch is the screen itself.
No host → the mind lines say so; the list still works.
diff --git a/src/code_red_eeg.c b/src/code_red_eeg.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..76250313
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/code_red_eeg.c
